    description: "The ATEEDGE is on this page to answer the under-$500 question honestly. It is the cheapest named-brand listing we found that states 10 mph, and it is a capable walking, incline-walking and jogging machine. The listing gives an 18.5 by 45.5-inch belt with shock absorption, a 3.0 HP motor reaching 10 mph, automatic incline up to 20% (2 to 8 degrees), a 350 lb weight capacity, 36 preset programmes, Bluetooth app connectivity and a 10 by 26-inch desk. The belt is the catch. At 45.5 inches it is shorter than the 50 to 55 inches we would want for running, and 18.5 inches is narrower than the 20 we recommend at speed, so a runner of average height will shorten their stride to fit it. Buy it as a jogging and incline machine, not as a running treadmill. Amazon listed it at $369.54 on 21 November 2026.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Best Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Best Budget Treadmills for Running", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-budget-treadmills-for-running/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the best low-cost treadmill for running?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The Horizon T101 Connect, at about $777 on Amazon on 21 November 2026. It has a 20 by 55-inch running area, 10 mph, 10% power incline and a lifetime frame and motor warranty. If you need to spend nearer $600, Sunny’s Auto Incline Treadmill gives a 20 by 53-inch surface and 10 mph.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the best running machine under $500?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "There is no true running treadmill under $500 in our view, because nothing we found at that price pairs a 20-inch belt with a length of 50 inches or more. The cheapest machine that reaches 10 mph is the ATEEDGE at about $370, but its 18.5 by 45.5-inch belt makes it a jogging machine. The BORGUSI at about $570 is the cheapest with a 20-inch belt.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the best treadmill for runners on a budget?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For most runners, the Horizon T101 Connect or the NordicTrack T 6.5 S, both with a 20 by 55-inch belt and 10 mph. The Horizon has the stronger motor warranty (lifetime); the NordicTrack is about $160 cheaper and works with iFIT. Runners over about 5 foot 10 should save for a 60-inch deck instead.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you run on a cheap treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "You can jog on many of them, but most cheap treadmills are built for walking. Check three things before you buy: a belt at least 20 inches wide and 50 to 55 inches long, a top speed of 10 mph, and a motor warranty stated in writing. The word “running” in a listing title is not a specification.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What top speed do I need on a treadmill for running?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Ten mph, a 6-minute mile, covers almost every home runner, including most interval work. An 8 mph ceiling is a 7:30 mile, fine for easy running but limiting for faster repeats. Only choose a 12 mph machine if your fastest intervals are quicker than 6:00 per mile.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is 3.0 HP enough for running on a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It is if it is 3.0 continuous horsepower (CHP), which is the figure our horsepower guide suggests for running. Most budget listings do not say whether their figure is continuous or peak, and a peak figure can be much higher than what the motor sustains. Without a CHP rating, judge the motor by its warranty.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a walking pad good for running?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. Most walking pads top out at 4 mph, and 2-in-1 pads with a handle reach about 6 to 7.5 mph on belts around 40 to 50 inches long and 16 to 17 inches wide. That suits walking and a light jog. For running, start at the 20-inch belts on this page.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-21",
      dateModified: "2026-11-28",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              ...(product.amazonUrl ? { url: product.amazonUrl } : {}),
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 6,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-budget-treadmills-for-running/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/best-budget-treadmills-for-running/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "best");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const GROUP_PAGES = GROUP?.pages ?? [];
const HERE_AT = GROUP_PAGES.findIndex((p) => p.url === HERE);
// The group's first 2 pages (its leads), then the pages after this one, wrapping round, so every page in a long
// hub group gets sibling links and the leads keep theirs (PLAYBOOK §0b L1).
const MORE = [...new Set([...GROUP_PAGES.slice(0, 2), ...GROUP_PAGES.slice(HERE_AT + 1), ...GROUP_PAGES.slice(0, Math.max(HERE_AT, 0))])].filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
